@Bradley
I didn't interpret Sean as saying that it was a copper patina, but as referring to the several different definitions and the Did You Know section in the Merriam-Webster entry for "patina." 

I confess I was more familiar with the M-W definitions 1a and 1b than the Le Creuset definition, although Le Creuset makes total sense and I'm going to start saying "patina" instead of "seasoned layer" when referring to what I occasionally mess up on my grandmother's skillets, which I gratefully inherited.

